  <h1>Press</h1>
  <p>Contact: <a href="mailto:contact@totalrecalls.app">contact@totalrecalls.app</a>.</p>

  <h2>What TotalRecalls is</h2>
  <p>TotalRecalls is a Windows desktop app that downloads your conversation history from eight AI assistants — ChatGPT, Claude, Perplexity, Gemini, Grok, DeepSeek, Mistral and Qwen Chat — and saves it as ordinary Markdown and JSON files on your own computer. It is a one-time $24 purchase with no subscription, no account, and no cloud service. An optional add-on, Smart Search Engine (SSE), searches that local library in plain English.</p>
  <p>The product exists because chat histories are the one part of an AI workflow that is still locked inside each provider: split across eight accounts, formatted eight different ways, and deleted or altered on the provider's schedule rather than yours. TotalRecalls turns them into a folder of files that opens in ten years, whatever happens to the accounts.</p>

  <h2>Facts</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Platform:</strong> Windows 10 and 11, 64-bit. Available via Microsoft Store or standalone portable build.</li>
    <li><strong>Price:</strong> Downloader Pro $24 USD, one-time (regular $48). Smart Search Engine (SSE) add-on $29 (regular $58); Downloader Pro + Smart Search Engine (SSE) bundle $49 (regular $98). A Free Tier covers three providers and five conversations per provider.</li>
    <li><strong>Data handling:</strong> everything stays on the customer's machine. No telemetry, no upload, no account with us.</li>
    <li><strong>Maker:</strong> a one-person software project based in Montreal, Quebec.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Assets</h2>
  <p>Logo and screenshots are available on request — write to <a href="mailto:contact@totalrecalls.app">contact@totalrecalls.app</a> and say what you need and in what format.</p>
